  "notes": "{愚痴|ぐち}る is a casual verb formed from the noun ⟦{愚痴|ぐち}→愚痴：06623_guchi⟧ (complaint/grumbling) by adding the verb ending る. This is a common word-formation pattern in colloquial Japanese.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is an informal/colloquial word. In formal contexts, use ⟦{愚痴|ぐち}を{言|い}う→愚痴を言う：25447_guchiwoiu⟧ or ⟦{不満|ふまん}→不満：02497_fuman⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{言|い}う→言う：00515_iu⟧.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～⟦について→〜について：03103_nitsuite⟧{愚痴|ぐち}る: to gripe about something\n- ～⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{愚痴|ぐち}る: to complain to someone\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n⟦{愚痴|ぐち}→愚痴：06623_guchi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{聞|き}く→聞く：00483_kiku⟧ means \"to listen to someone's complaints.\"",
